      "hints": [
        "Find the $x^2$ and $x^3$ terms in $(1-2x)^5$.",
        "Form the coefficient equation $40k - 80 = 20$.",
        "Solve for $k$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Find the $x^2$ and $x^3$ terms in the binomial expansion of $(1 - 2x)^5$:\n$$\\text{Term in } x^2:\\quad \\binom{5}{2}(1)^3(-2x)^2 = 10(4x^2) = 40x^2$$\n$$\\text{Term in } x^3:\\quad \\binom{5}{3}(1)^2(-2x)^3 = 10(-8x^3) = -80x^3$$",
        "Identify the products from $(1 + kx)(1 - 2x)^5$ that produce an $x^3$ term:\n$$1 \\times (-80x^3) = -80x^3$$\n$$kx \\times (40x^2) = 40kx^3$$",
        "Equate the combined coefficient of $x^3$ to $20$:\n$$40k - 80 = 20$$",
        "Solve for the constant $k$:\n$$40k = 100 \\implies k = \\frac{100}{40} = 2.5 = \\frac{5}{2}$$"
      ],
